2. Contact page — final behaviour

The Contact page intentionally uses three direct contact methods:

Email

The Open email draft / Send enquiry action uses a mailto: URL.

The form collects:

Full name

Work email

Company

Message

The website then creates a pre-filled email addressed to the sales email configured in src/data/site.js.

Example draft:

To
sales@nexora.ai

Subject
Nexora enquiry — Acme

Body

Hello Nexora team,

I would like to discuss my workflows and learn more about Nexora.

Name: Rishabh Verma
Work email: rishabh@example.com
Company: Acme

Message:
We want to automate lead routing.

Regards,
Rishabh Verma

Important

A mailto: link does not send the email automatically.

It asks the browser/operating system to open the user's configured email application or webmail handler with a new, pre-filled draft. The user must still press Send in that email application. This is the expected behaviour of the mailto: scheme. citehttps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Structuring_content/Creating_links

If no email application is configured for mailto:, the browser may not open a compose window. Keep the visible sales email address on the page as a fallback.

WhatsApp

The WhatsApp cards and the WhatsApp instead action open the configured WhatsApp contact and start a direct conversation.

Phone

The phone action uses a tel: link. On compatible mobile devices it can open the dialer; behaviour on desktop depends on the installed call application.

3. Recommended Contact wording

Use language that is honest about what the static V1 site does.

Preferred primary button:

Open email draft

Supporting text:

Opens your email app with a pre-filled enquiry.

Good success/status message:

Your email draft should now be open.
Review the details and press Send in your email app.

Avoid:

“Your enquiry has been received.”

That wording would imply that the website has actually transmitted the enquiry to a backend when this V1 does not.

